}

templ opensearchInvertedIndexGuide() {
	@docH2("inverted", "Inverted indexes")
	@docP() {
		An inverted index maps every token produced by an analyzer to the list of document IDs (postings list) where that token appears, along with term frequencies and positions. When you search for a phrase or a partial name, OpenSearch intersects postings lists instead of scanning every document.
	}
	@docH2("mappings", "text vs keyword fields")
	@docP() {
		Always define explicit mappings before indexing production data. Use @docCodeWord("text") on fields you search with full-text queries (analyzed and lowercased) and @docCodeWord("keyword") on fields you filter, sort, or aggregate verbatim (makes, cities, status codes).
	}
	@docCode("mapping.json", opensearchMappingCode)
	@docH2("refresh", "Near-real-time refresh and shards")
	@docP() {
		New writes land in an in-memory buffer and transaction log first, then become searchable after a Lucene segment refresh (every 1 second by default, or immediately with @docCodeWord("refresh=wait_for") on the write request). On a single-node lab, set @docCodeWord("number_of_replicas: 0") so every index reaches green health instead of waiting for a second node to hold replicas.
	}
}

templ opensearchQueriesGuide() {
	@docH2("context", "Query vs filter context")
	@docP() {
		Inside a @docCodeWord("bool") query, put full-text search terms under @docCodeWord("must") so Lucene computes BM25 relevance scores, and put exact constraints (EV type, model year, range thresholds) under @docCodeWord("filter") where clauses skip scoring and reuse Lucene's bitset filter cache.
	}
	@docCode("search.json", opensearchQueryCode)
	@docH2("facets", "Faceted aggregations")
	@docP() {
		Aggregations run over doc values of @docCodeWord("keyword") and numeric fields alongside the query, returning bucket counts (such as registrations per make or electric range bands) in a single round trip.
	}
	@docH2("errors", "Handling partial bulk errors in v5")
	@docP() {
		The official @docCodeWord("opensearch-go/v5") client surfaces partial bulk and shard failures as typed Go errors instead of hiding them inside an HTTP 200 payload. Always inspect bulk responses and use deterministic document IDs so retrying a batch is idempotent.
	}
}

templ opensearchCDCAliasGuide() {
	@docH2("cqrs", "Postgres to Kafka to OpenSearch")
	@docP() {
		Keep transactional writes in Postgres and publish keyed change events to Kafka (partitioned by entity ID to preserve per-record ordering). A dedicated projector consumes batches, writes to OpenSearch with Bulk requests, and commits Kafka offsets only after OpenSearch acknowledges the batch. If the search index is ever lost or its schema changes, resetting the consumer group to offset 0 rebuilds it completely from the log.
	}
	@docH2("aliases", "Atomic alias swaps and _reindex")
	@docP() {
		Because field types in an existing OpenSearch mapping cannot be changed in place, point application reads and writes at an index alias rather than a physical index name. To migrate mappings without downtime, create the new versioned index, copy documents with @docCodeWord("_reindex")&#44; and swap the alias atomically in one @docCodeWord("_aliases") call:
	}
	@docCode("aliases.json", opensearchAliasSwapCode)
}

templ opensearchInBreadboardGuide() {
	@docH2("tls", "TLS on HTTP and loopback transport")
	@docP() {
		Breadboard runs @docCodeWord("opensearchproject/opensearch:3.10.0") in single-node mode with the Security plugin enabled and demo certificates disabled. Port @docCodeWord("9200") serves HTTPS using the service's lab certificate and sets @docCodeWord("http.publish_host") to the service FQDN so client node discovery verifies TLS cleanly. Transport port @docCodeWord("9300") stays bound strictly to @docCodeWord("127.0.0.1") inside the container.
	}
	@docCode("experiment.yaml", opensearchSpecYAML)
	@docH2("env", "What your app receives")
	@docP() {
		Any app with @docCodeWord("opensearch") in @docCodeWord("uses") receives @docCodeWord("OPENSEARCH_URL")&#44; @docCodeWord("OPENSEARCH_USER")&#44; @docCodeWord("OPENSEARCH_PASSWORD")&#44; and @docCodeWord("OPENSEARCH_CACERT") — plus @docCodeWord("SSL_CERT_FILE") automatically. Connect directly with the official Go client:
	}
	@docCode("main.go", opensearchClientCode)
	@docH2("explore", "The Indices tab")
	@docP() {
		Open the OpenSearch service page in @docCodeWord("bb serve") and switch to the <strong>Indices</strong> tab (or call the @docCodeWord("opensearch_indices") MCP tool) to inspect cluster status, shard counts, user indices, doc counts, storage sizes, and active aliases.
	}
}
